# Visibility Offering — Cash Flow (CF) Module Spec

_Source of truth: the Excel workbook (CF tab, plus upstream Flow, Financial Structure, Organizational Structure, Salaries & Benefits, Budget). This file consolidates the rules captured there + clarifications, in the same shape as the Budget Module Spec._

---

## 0. Placement in the Vision & Virtue website

- Sections **1 → 20** of this spec render in the website under **"4. CF Structure"**, immediately after **"3. Budget"** (the Budget Module).
- Sections **21 → 22** render under **"5. CF Forecast"**.
- Section **23** renders under **"6. CF Dashboard"**.
- The CF module is **per-budget**: each finalized budget (Section 5.4 of the Budget Spec) has its own CF. The user picks an active budget before entering the CF flow.
- Inherits from the active budget: **Year**, **Period granularity** (Monthly / Quarterly / Yearly), **Currency**, **Scale**. CF cannot change these — to change, the user edits the budget.
- Cap and storage: a CF is part of the budget it belongs to (no separate 5-budget cap; deleting the budget deletes its CF).

---

## 1. Source dataset (the "budget metrics")

The CF reads from the finalized Budget Structure of the active budget. Each budget row is one unique combination of:

> **Company + Service Provider Name + Service Description + Division + Department + Product + Activity + Account/GL Name + Account/GL Number + P&L Section + Budget Category** + period amounts (Jan-2X … Dec-2X, or quarters / FY depending on granularity).

This is treated as a **pivot-style dataset**. All CF allocations below aggregate (SUM) period amounts over a chosen subset of these dimension columns. No CF screen mutates the budget data; CF only reads.

Sign convention used everywhere in the CF module:
- **Costs** in the budget (COGS, R&D, S&M, G&A) are stored as **positive** numbers; in CF expense rows they are shown as **positive debit movement** and the matching **payments** are shown as **negative** (cash leaving).
- **Revenues** in the budget are stored as **negative** numbers (per the CF tab example); in CF revenue rows they are shown as **negative credit movement** and the matching **collections** are shown as **positive** (cash entering).
- Balances on liabilities (Payables, Salaries & Benefits opening balance) are presented as **negative in parentheses** `($X,XXX)`.
- Balances on assets (Receivables, Inventory, Cash) are presented as **positive** `$X,XXX`.

