## 4. WC → Receivables

### 4.1 Opening Balance

On `+` next to **Receivables**, an **O.B** field appears. The user enters the opening A/R balance as a plain positive number, displayed as `$X,XXX` (debit balance).

### 4.2 Allocation scope

Receivables covers **all Revenues** in the budget: rows where `P&L Section = "Revenues"`. Revenue amounts in the budget are negative; in the CF Receivables grid the **Revenue** row is shown as negative (credit movement) and the **Payment** (collection) row is shown as positive (cash in).

### 4.3 Allocation columns (left → right)

Same incremental-breakdown UX as Payables (§3.3), with **Customer Name** as the deepest level instead of Service Provider Name.

| Step | Columns shown |
|---|---|
| Default | Company → Budget Section |
| +GL | Company → Budget Section → Account/GL Name |
| +Customer | Company → Budget Section → GL → Customer Name |

**Customer Name** is sourced from the budget's `Service Provider Name` column for Revenue rows (in the budget the buyer is recorded there — see CF tab example rows 6–7). The CF surfaces it relabeled as "Customer Name". Unallocated-residual auto-rows behave the same way as Payables.

Table columns: `Company | Budget Section | GL | Customer Name | Payment terms | Jan-2X … Dec-2X | FY-2X total`.

### 4.4 Revenue + Payment rows

| Type | Source | Sign |
|---|---|---|
| **Revenue** | SUM of period amounts from the budget dataset for that combination | Negative (credit movement; matches budget storage) |
| **Payment** | Computed from Revenue row using row's chosen Payment terms (same dropdown as §3.6) | Positive (cash in) |
### 4.5 Payment formula (canonical)

Same as Payables (§3.7) with sign flipped for cash-in:

```
Payment[m] = - Revenue[m - lag]   if (m - lag) is within the budget year   (Revenue is stored negative, so this yields a positive cash-in)
Payment[m] = "Enter Free amount"   if (m - lag) is before the budget start
Payment[m] = 0   if there is no matching revenue in that lagged month
```

### 4.6 Customers summary table (auto)

Once all payment-terms cells are set, the **Customers summary** renders:

| Row | Per-month formula |
|---|---|
| **O.B** | Jan: amount set in §4.1, positive. Feb–Dec: previous month's C.B. |
| **Revenues** | SUM of Revenue rows for the month, displayed **positive** (debit movement — A/R increases). |
| **Payment** | SUM of Payment rows for the month, displayed **negative in parentheses** (credit movement — A/R decreases). |
| **C.B** | `O.B + Revenues − Payment` (with signs as above, result is positive debit balance). |

FY column = sum across months (for O.B / C.B = Jan O.B and Dec C.B respectively).

