## 5. WC → Inventory

### 5.1 Opening Balance

On `+` next to **Inventory**, an **O.B** field appears. Entered as a plain positive number, displayed `$X,XXX` (debit balance).

### 5.2 No allocation grid

Unlike Payables / Receivables, Inventory has **no per-row allocation**. Only the summary table below is shown.

### 5.3 Inventory summary table

| Row | Per-month formula |
|---|---|
| **O.B** | Jan: amount set in §5.1, positive. Feb–Dec: previous month's C.B. |
| **Purchases** | **Free user input** per month (positive). The field starts empty and requires entry. This same Purchases stream feeds the **Finished goods** Expense row in Payables (§3.5). |
| **COGS** | Auto-pulled from the budget: the **Finished goods** Budget Category under the **COGS** P&L Section for that month. Displayed as **negative** (credit movement — inventory consumed). |
| **C.B** | `O.B + Purchases + COGS` (Purchases positive, COGS negative). |

Validation: if `C.B` would go below 0 in any month, show a non-blocking warning ("Inventory goes negative in <month>. Increase Purchases or check COGS mapping.").

