## 6. Salaries & Benefits (CF)

### 6.1 Opening Balance

On `+` next to **Salaries & Benefits**, an **O.B** field appears — the closing accrued salary liability from the prior year. Entered positive, displayed as **negative in parentheses** `($X,XXX)` (credit balance).

### 6.2 Summary table

Only a single summary table — no per-vendor allocation. Salaries flow as a single block per month.

| Row | Per-month formula |
|---|---|
| **O.B** | Jan: amount from §6.1, shown `($X,XXX)`. Feb–Dec: previous month's C.B. |
| **Expenses** | Auto-pulled from the budget: **SUM of all rows with `Budget Category = "Salaries and benefits"`** for that month (across COGS / R&D / S&M / G&A). Positive in the table (the credit-movement sign convention is applied to C.B). |
| **Payment** | Jan: **free user input** (positive number) representing payment for the prior December (the O.B drawdown). Feb–Dec: auto = **− Expenses of the previous month** (salaries are paid one month in arrears, fixed). |
| **C.B** | `O.B + Expenses(as credit) − Payment` → `($X,XXX)`. |

Payment terms are **fixed at "30+" (one-month arrears)** for salaries — no per-row terms dropdown. The Jan field is the only free input.

