## 11. CF Forecast (under website section "5. CF Forecast")

### 11.1 View controls

Three independent toggles at the top of the Forecast view:

| Control | Options | Behavior |
|---|---|---|
| **Period** | Monthly / Quarterly / FY | Re-aggregates all rows. Monthly→Quarterly sums Jan+Feb+Mar etc.; Quarterly→FY sums Q1+Q2+Q3+Q4. |
| **Scale** | Standard / Thousands | Display only — underlying values untouched. Thousands separator always shown. |
| **Burn detail** | Collapsed / Expanded | Collapsed: single **Burn** row. Expanded: three rows — Adjusted EBITDA, WC, Other Adjustments. Toggle via `+`/`–` next to the Burn label. |

### 11.2 Main CF table (Monthly view shown)

| Row | Per-month formula | FY column |
|---|---|---|
| **O.B** | Jan: amount from §2 row 1 (Opening Cash). Feb–Dec: previous month's C.B. | Jan O.B value. |
| **Adjusted EBITDA** | SUM(budget rows) per month where P&L ∈ {Revenues, COGS, R&D, S&M, G&A}. **Includes all rows, including `Budget Category = "Salaries and benefits"`** — salaries expenses stay inside EBITDA. (Revenues negative + Costs positive = the operating burn, shown as a single signed number per month.) | Sum across months. |
| **WC** | `− (ΔPayables + ΔReceivables + ΔInventory)` per month, i.e. the cash impact of WC movements. **Salaries Δliability is excluded from WC** — it is shown as its own Forecast row below. See §12 for the underlying breakdown. | Sum across months. |
| **Salaries & Benefits** | `− (Salaries.C.B(m) − Salaries.C.B(m−1))` per month, where the Salaries C.B / O.B come from the §6 Salaries summary block (O.B + Expense − Payment = C.B, all in the credit-balance convention of §6). For January, `m−1` C.B = the Salaries O.B (per §6.1). This formula gives the **cash adjustment that converts the salary expense inside Adjusted EBITDA into actual salary cash paid**: it adds back the expense (already in EBITDA) and subtracts the payment. **No double-count occurs** because EBITDA includes the expense and this row reverses it back to the cash figure. **It is not a WC component** — it is its own Forecast row. | Sum across months. |
| **Other Adjustments** | Footer Total row from §7 for that month. | Sum across months. |
| **Burn (collapsed)** | `Adjusted EBITDA + WC + Salaries & Benefits + Other Adjustments` per month. Used when the user collapses the four sub-rows. | Sum across months. |
| **Financing** | Footer Total row from §8 for that month. | Sum across months. |
| **Capex** | Footer Total row from §9 for that month. | Sum across months. |
| **C.B** | `O.B + Adjusted EBITDA + WC + Salaries & Benefits + Other Adjustments + Financing + Capex`. | Dec C.B. |

Salaries are treated as their **own Forecast row**, separate from WC. Salaries expenses **remain inside Adjusted EBITDA** (they are not stripped out). The Salaries Forecast row is the **balance-sheet movement of the salary liability** between each month's C.B and O.B in the §6 Salaries summary: `− (C.B − O.B)` per month. Because the §6 summary embeds the full salary expense (via the Expense row pulled from the budget) and the actual payment, this single movement number already does the EBITDA-to-cash conversion for salaries: it adds back the non-cash expense and reflects only the cash payment. The WC row (§12) excludes the salaries-liability movement to avoid duplicating this adjustment.

Sign formatting: all rows show positive `$X,XXX` and negative `($X,XXX)`.
### 11.3 Aggregation when Period control changes

- Monthly → Quarterly: each row's quarter = sum of its three months. O.B(Q1) = Jan O.B; C.B(Q1) = Mar C.B.
- Quarterly → FY: O.B(FY) = Jan O.B; C.B(FY) = Dec C.B; movement rows sum all months.

