## 12. WC breakdown table (under the main CF, same screen)

Renders below the main CF table on "5. CF Forecast". One row per WC component, computed from the summary tables in §3, §4, §5.

| Row | Per-month formula |
|---|---|
| **Payables** | `− (Payables.C.B(m) − Payables.C.B(m-1))`. An increase in A/P liability is a **positive** cash impact (we owe more, paid less). Sign of the displayed number follows the cash-impact convention: positive `$X,XXX` if A/P grew, negative `($X,XXX)` if A/P shrank. |
| **Receivables** | `− (Receivables.C.B(m) − Receivables.C.B(m-1))`. An increase in A/R is a **negative** cash impact (customers owe us more, collected less). |
| **Inventory** | `− (Inventory.C.B(m) − Inventory.C.B(m-1))`. Inventory build = negative cash impact; drawdown = positive cash impact. |
| **Total** | SUM of the three above (Payables + Receivables + Inventory only — **salaries are not in WC**). This equals the **WC** row in §11.2. |

For January: `m-1` C.B is the **O.B** of that section (per §3.8 / §4.6 / §5.3).

FY column = sum of months for movement rows; Total FY must reconcile to `Dec C.B − O.B` of each section's summary (audit check).

