## 16. Resolved decisions (formerly TBD)
- **Salaries treatment:** Salaries are a **separate row in the CF Forecast**, sitting between WC and Other Adjustments (§11.2). Salaries expenses **remain inside Adjusted EBITDA** (no filter is applied to EBITDA). Salaries are **not** in WC. The Salaries Forecast row sources from the §6 Salaries summary as `− (C.B_salaries(m) − C.B_salaries(m−1))` — the end-of-month-to-end-of-month movement of the salary liability. Because §6 builds C.B as `O.B + Expense − Payment` (credit-balance convention), this single movement number already converts the salary expense embedded in EBITDA into the actual cash paid: it implicitly adds back the expense and subtracts the payment. No double-count. The WC row excludes the salaries-liability Δ to avoid duplicating this conversion. Salaries are **not** routed through the Payables cycle and are **not** subject to per-row payment terms — §6 hard-codes one-month arrears (Jan Payment settles prior Dec; Feb–Dec Payment = prior month's Expense).
- **Finished goods linkage:** the Payables `Expense` row for `Budget Category = Finished goods` is overridden to pull from Inventory.Purchases (§3.5 / §5.3). The budget's own Finished-goods line is what feeds Inventory.COGS — it is **not** double-counted in Payables.
- **Re-finalization of the budget:** if the user edits the active budget after the CF is finalized, the CF re-reads the dataset on next open. Auto-rows and computed rows refresh. Any manual rows whose dimension combo no longer exists in the budget become **orphan CF rows** with a banner: _"N CF row(s) reference combinations no longer in the budget. Review or delete in <section>."_
- **Currency / scale change:** CF inherits live from the budget; no FX conversion (same rule as Budget §6).
- **CF deletion:** deleting the parent budget deletes its CF. No standalone CF delete.
- **Cap:** no separate CF cap; constrained by the 5-budget cap on the parent budget.
